# The main story's scenes (24 Nov 2026): the Custodians, Zachary's plan (docs/story/CUSTODIANS.md). Played by
# scripts/cutscene.gd like the heart events and HeartEvents.SCENES, with the same steps, plus the picture panels
# ("board", "bsprite", "bmove", "bmoves", "bfade", "flash"; see cutscene.gd) for what happens off the station.
# main.gd starts each one when the story calls for it. tests/check_heart_events.py checks them too.
#
# A scene can open on a picture instead of the map: "board" is the picture shown as the scene fades in, and
# "board_setup" the sprites already on it.
#
# Off-station voices: "Ivan" (his portrait), "MotherDrone" (art/portrait_motherdrone.png), and narration with a
# name and no face (["say", "", lines, "Ship computer"]).
#
# The lines are Claude's, from Zachary's prologue script (docs/story/PROLOGUE_SCRIPT.md, scenes 1-3) and his plan
# of 24 Nov: the Mother-Drone "beams part of itself into your mind allowing you to talk with other alien artifacts".

# Pictures used (paths are written out in full so tests/check_heart_events.py can read the scenes):
#   res://art/ships/needle/needle_*.png      the Wandering Star: the artist's own Needle, 80 x 55, whole and without
#                                            her starboard wing; shown only at whole sizes (3x in the prologue, 2x
#                                            in the storm) so her pixels stay crisp
#   res://art/ships/ivan_flagship/hull.png   the Rabble's Crown
#
# The Custodians' sound (25 Nov, Zachary: the bell was "too loud and harsh and not mysterious musical"): "custodian_call",
# a soft swell of glass tones (tools/dev/custodian_sounds.py), at a different pitch for each, a musical step apart:
# the three in the museum and the vision 1.0; the Harbinger 0.8409 (three semitones down, of the deep rock); the
# Shepherd 0.8909 (a tone down); the lullaby 0.7492 (a fourth down, so slower and lower); the Warden 1.1225 (a tone up).
#   res://art/ships/fx/hit.png               6 frames of 48 x 48;  fire.png: 4 frames of 24 x 24
#   res://art/prologue/*.png                 tools/dev/prologue_art.py (space, the moon from the menu's art, glyphs),
#                                            tools/dev/crash_site_art.py (the drone's animation, the beam, the light
#                                            through the roof, the grit, lined up with the crash site's props)

